OpenEXR-rs

A Rust port of OpenEXR (https://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr).
Each release states the OpenEXR version it matches; this line matches
OpenEXR 3.5.3 (upstream tag v3.5.3, commit 3950290530c4fd4776667d0dc4d65a9d003eb936).

The port is a derivative work of OpenEXR and is distributed under the same
BSD-3-Clause license (see LICENSE):

    Copyright Contributors to the OpenEXR Project.

Test data generated by the oracle comes from the official OpenEXR 3.5.3 Python
wheel (PyPI: openexr==3.5.3). Tests and test images ported from upstream keep
upstream's BSD-3-Clause license and notice.

DreamWorks Lossy Compression (DWAA/DWAB) is offered by upstream under the terms
of upstream's PATENTS file (upstream/openexr/PATENTS), which a port of it carries.

Third-party code
----------------

OpenEXRCore is built with code vendored under upstream/openexr/external, each
under its own license: libdeflate v1.26 (MIT), zstd v1.5.7 (BSD; upstream zstd
is dual-licensed, and the vendored copy carries the BSD license) and OpenJPH
0.32.0 (BSD-2-Clause). THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md will carry each
notice in the chunk that first translates that library.
